From 590e36795245a4abff2e29b53ce82858eb5bd566 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rickow <30348240+Rickow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:24:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HSFA: SFA3 mirrored sprite tiles (flip flag in the object
 tables)

The SFA3 object tables (f<N>, built by banques.py) turn a local tile of the
PS2 port into a code of the arcade graphics ROM by matching the content
EXACTLY. The port stores some tiles flipped: they have no exact match, the
entry stayed empty and HsfaEclater dropped the tile (holes in sprites:
1,084 non-empty tiles over 17 Arcade runs, e.g. Dhalsim's legs in the
intro).

Translator v157 (OBJ_MIROIR, on by default, SFA3 only) now fills these
entries with the ROM tile and the flip to apply: bit 29 = X, bit 30 = Y
(1,311 entries in 44 tables). HsfaEclater masks the code to 20 bits and
XORs the flag into the attribute of the 16x16 tile it emits (bits 5-6).

Tables without the flag bits (Upper, Upper MAX, Hyper, graft, SFA3 before
v157) give exactly the same output as before. A core without this patch
shows these tiles unflipped: ship the tables with this patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/burn/drv/capcom/cps_hsfa.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/burn/drv/capcom/cps_hsfa.cpp b/src/burn/drv/capcom/cps_hsfa.cpp
index ae92075..6fc77e6 100644
--- a/src/burn/drv/capcom/cps_hsfa.cpp
+++ b/src/burn/drv/capcom/cps_hsfa.cpp
@@ -389,6 +389,10 @@ static UINT16 HsfaEclater(UINT32 nPage, UINT32 nFin, UINT32 nCourante)
 				INT32 cx = fx ? (nx - 1 - nxs) : nxs;
 				INT32 cy = fy ? (ny - 1 - nys) : nys;
 				INT32 g = HsfaGlobal(t, code + cx + 16 * cy);
+				// (patch 0024) SFA3 : tuile que le portage range en MIROIR (absente de la ROM a l'identique) : la table
+				// donne la tuile de la ROM et le retournement a appliquer (bit 29 = X, bit 30 = Y), XORe dans l'attribut
+				UINT16 fl = 0;
+				if (g >= 0) { fl = (UINT16)((g >> 24) & 0x60); g &= 0xFFFFF; }
 				if (g >= 0) {
 					if (n < 1023) {
 						// (HANDOFF §116) bits 16-17 -> Y 13-14 ; bits 18-19 -> X 10-11
@@ -399,7 +403,7 @@ static UINT16 HsfaEclater(UINT32 nPage, UINT32 nFin, UINT32 nCourante)
 						if (((y >> 13) & 7) == 1) Out[n * 4 + 1] |= 0x1000;	// (patch 0023) emplacement 1 (graphismes systeme : HUD)
 #endif
 						Out[n * 4 + 2] = (UINT16)(g & 0xffff);
-						Out[n * 4 + 3] = (UINT16)(at & 0x00ff);
+						Out[n * 4 + 3] = (UINT16)((at ^ fl) & 0x00ff);
 						n++;
 					}
 					nTotal++;
